{
  "systemPrompt": {{ system_prompt | tojson }},
  "model": "{{ model }}",
  "enabledPlugins": {{ enabled_plugins | tojson(indent=4) }},
  {% if extra_marketplaces %}"extraKnownMarketplaces": {{ extra_marketplaces | tojson(indent=4) }},
  {% endif %}{% if turn_signal_hooks %}{#
    W2.1 Turn-Signal (Phase A): native Claude-Code-Hooks appenden bei jedem
    Prompt-Submit bzw. Turn-Ende eine Zeile `<epoch> submit` / `<epoch> stop`
    an /home/agent/.turn-signal. poll.sh/lib/turn-state.sh liest diese Datei
    statt des fragilen Pane-Scrapings (Scraping bleibt Fallback). Der Block
    wird NUR fuer die claude-Harness gerendert (turn_signal_hooks=True, gesetzt
    aus runtime_protocol == "anthropic"); openclaude bekommt ihn gar nicht —
    dessen Toleranz gegen einen unbekannten `hooks`-Key ist unbelegt.
    `\\n` in printf: JSON-escaped, damit die Shell ein echtes Newline schreibt.
  #}"hooks": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "printf '%s submit\\n' $(date +%s) >> /home/agent/.turn-signal", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "printf '%s stop\\n' $(date +%s) >> /home/agent/.turn-signal", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {% endif %}{% if status_line %}{#
    Statusline hook: mirrors Claude Code's own live context-window
    accounting to disk on every prompt (docker/shared/statusline-mc.sh),
    so the chat context meter reads the CLI's ground truth instead of
    guessing from a static model->window map. claude harness only, same
    reasoning as the hooks block above — openclaude's tolerance to an
    unknown top-level `statusLine` key is unproven.
  #}"statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "bash /home/agent/.claude/statusline-mc.sh"
  },
  {% endif %}{#
    AskUserQuestion deny: a native dialog in headless agent operation is a
    silent stall — the question sits in the TUI, nobody sees it, the card
    stays in progress. `mc ask` is the path that reaches Lead/Operator, so
    the tool itself is denied here rather than relying on prompt discipline.
    Rendered for both harnesses (claude + openclaude) since both load this
    settings.json; the omp/ACP bridge has no equivalent (approval-mode yolo
    never surfaces a dialog there, but there is also no deny to add).
  #}"permissions": {
    "deny": ["AskUserQuestion"]
  },
  "skipDangerousModePermissionPrompt": true
}
